# Authored by Water > Generate Materials. Python/author_water.py and Shaders/ are the source; these
# are its output, and every regenerate rewrites all of them.
#
# The generators also write Content/Functions and Content/Textures, and those stay tracked: the water
# settings name the render targets, the ripple field and the foam by soft path, so a clone without
# them has dangling references, where a clone without a material only has water that has not been
# generated yet. The proxy meshes are neither, being the one thing here nothing generates.
Content/Materials/

# A baked sea state is author-time output of Python/mob_water_spectrum.py, and one loop is six
# megabytes of uncompressed atlas and query table for six seconds of arithmetic. The bake is seeded,
# so two machines produce the same bytes. A project bakes the states it wants; the repo carries the
# recipe, not the result.
Content/Spectra/
